{"segs": ["PA_ja_183:0.1"], "en": "Jātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_183:0.2", "PA_ja_183:0.3"], "en": "The Second Book of Pairs (Dukanipāta), Chapter on the Peerless (Asadisavagga)", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_183:0.4"], "en": "3. The Vālodaka Jātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_183:1.1", "PA_ja_183:1.2"], "en": "“Having drunk the scant and inferior water of a hair-tuft, intoxication arises in the donkeys.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_183:1.3"], "en": "“Having drunk this exquisite flavor,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_183:1.4"], "en": "no intoxication arises in Sindh horses.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_183:2.1"], "en": "“Having drunk only a little, one of low birth...”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_183:2.2"], "en": "Thus, O Lord of Men, when asked,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_183:2.3", "PA_ja_183:2.4"], "en": "I say: One who is of steadfast virtue and born of a noble family does not become intoxicated even after drinking the finest liquor.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_183:3.1"], "en": "The Vālodakajātaka, the third.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"}
]
